SPU: position-independent code modules: lifted once, dispatched wherever they are loaded.

Resistance 3's job igjob_00DC0200 loads two small modules (guest 0xDB2D80 and 0xDB0400) into its local store at a
new address every time (0x11B60, 0x133C0, 0x146C0, ...) and calls them. A lift is made for one address, so they ran in
the interpreter: in the opening cutscene (the blurred hand) about 25M interpreted steps/s on two SPU threads, and the
game stood at 0-2 fps for 20-35 s; afterwards about 12M steps/s kept the cutscene at 25-28 fps instead of 30.
Their only references to their own addresses are pc-relative (lqr, link values, relative branches), so one lift serves
every load:

- spu_lifter.py --pic (build_spu_workloads.py --pic IMAGE): every LS address of the image that the code observes --
  lqr/stqr addresses, link values, return pcs, transfer targets -- is emitted moved by _pd, the load offset a function
  takes on entry from the pc it was entered at (ctx->pc is the entry's address on every way into a lifted function;
  the PIC lift sets it before its own direct calls). Absolute branches (bra/brasl) stay absolute. Without --pic the
  output is unchanged (all 62 SPU images of the title lift byte-identical).
- spu_overlay_register_pic_region: a verified region whose GET may land anywhere. The load at L takes a resident code
  slot: the one at L, else one whose whole span the GET overwrote, else a free one, else the one of another copy --
  one that later loads overwrote in part first, the oldest first (resident slots record when they were loaded). Copies
  neither use up the slots nor keep fixed-address code out, and one that a later load overwrote in part keeps the rest
  while a slot is free. (Evicting simply the oldest copy threw out the one the job had been running all along.) The copy is verified once against the code bytes moved to
  L, and dispatch to A there runs the function lifted at A - L + link address.

Test: tools/test_spu_lifter_pic.py lifts a module with --pic and runs it with the runtime at three load addresses (14
checks fail at the two non-zero ones without --pic); runtime/spu/tests/test_spu_lifted_start.c
test_pic_resident_code (8 checks fail without the address mapping).

Upstream: not proposed yet.

